WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-18, with W3


STATE

  Version 0.0.1, the skeleton, on branch dev, pushed. Follows the
  tam-idol 0.2.0 standard (W3). It runs simple commands with quoting, ;
  and newline lists, comments, PATH search and exit statuses, the
  builtins exit, cd, :, true and false, and -c, script and
  standard-input modes. Everything else (pipes, $x, if, redirections)
  is refused with a clear message, never approximated. readelf -d lists
  only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass: unit tests, script
  tests against bash --posix, and refusal tests.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5; tam-clam ships only its own key
  map (no built-in readline map), drafted in arch/keys.md and agreed with
  Fred before 0.2.0.


NEXT

  1. 0.0.2, pipelines and redirections (plans/P1-foundation.md):
     - parser nodes for pipelines (with !), and-or lists, and a
       redirection list on a simple command (src/parse.c,
       include/tam-clam/ast.h);
     - every redirection operator, with IO numbers and - to close;
     - here-documents read after the line's newline, kept in memory
       with a size cap;
     - redirections on builtins save and restore descriptors (src/exec.c);
     - the pipeline status is the last command's.
     Each refusal it replaces moves from tests/refuse/ to tests/scripts/,
     and every new behaviour gets a script test that must match bash
     --posix. Bump VERSION to 0.0.2 in the first code commit.

  2. 0.0.3, variables and parameter expansion; 0.0.4, compound commands
     and functions (plans/P1-foundation.md). 0.0.3 changes words from raw
     text to parts in the parser, while the code is still small.


